WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.790
Sodium sits at the left of period
3, and chlorine near the right.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.850
A chlorine atom has six more
electrons than a sodium atom.

3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.530
More electrons, so you
might expect a bigger atom.

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.370
But the chlorine atom is
the smaller of the two.

5
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.610
So why is a chlorine atom
smaller than a sodium atom,

6
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.950
even though it has six more electrons?

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.630
In this mission, you'll meet the three
factors that explain every periodic trend.

8
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.570
You'll follow the trends in
the sizes of atoms and ions,

9
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.910
in ionization energy, in electron
affinity and in electronegativity.

10
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: explain why a chlorine
atom is smaller than a sodium atom.
